  "query": "As someone who has witnessed the decline of local shopping centers and the rise of online shopping, help me analyze what's happening to retail as malls close down and more people shop online in the United States over the past two decades, with particular focus on changes since COVID-19 (i.e, since early 2020). I want to know (1) how these changes are affecting local community economies and jobs, (2) what's happening to all the empty stores and malls (both large shopping centers and smaller strip malls), (3) how people's shopping habits have really changed during this period, and (4) what creative solutions other communities have found to bring these abandoned retail spaces back to life. Show me real examples and case studies from American cities and towns, with as many references and data sources as you can find"
}
